  "description": "JP-8000 supersaw: four saws at ±7 and ±23 cents with spread 15 make eight saws per note at ±8, ±22 and ±38 cents, the outer pair quieter, as Szabo measured the JP-8000 at a Detune of about 0.7. Trance pad and chord layer — play C3–C5 in 3–4-note chords (eight saws are two voices per note; a 6-note chord fills the part), gate 0.5 s or longer; mod wheel adds vibrato and opens the filter. Mixer: the supersaw’s highpass is the low cut at 120 Hz; chorus light, rate 0.3 Hz, depth 1.5 ms, mix 0.25; plate send 0.35; sidechain the strip’s compressor to the kick.",
