  "description": "Roland Jupiter-8 strings: saw, a detuned pulse and a second saw with a touch of cross-modulation, brighter and cleaner than the OB, through the 24 dB lowpass with key tracking. Play C3–C6 in 3–4-note chords, gate 1 s or longer; velocity brightens, mod wheel adds vibrato and opens the filter. Mixer: the JP-8’s highpass is the strip’s low cut at 180 Hz; chorus rate 0.7 Hz, depth 2 ms, spread 0.9, mix 0.4; plate send 0.3.",
