  "tags": ["lead", "sync", "width", "sweep", "original"],
  "description": "Operator width as a sync-style sweep: a sine squeezed to a fifth of its period at note-on, opened to the plain wave by LFO 2 (one-shot saw down, unipolar, 0.4 Hz, so the sweep takes about 2.5 s), with a sine an octave up for body and a 24 dB lowpass whose envelope follows. Play single notes C3–C5, gate 1–3 s; every new note restarts the sweep, and the mod wheel adds vibrato. Mixer: echo send 0.25, plate 0.2.",
